; A spec whose SCOPES reference each other. Legal on the rust face (rust modules may reference each
; other freely) and rejected under `--component`: each scope becomes one WIT interface, and WIT
; requires `use`-linked interfaces to be acyclic.
;
; The cycle is deliberately INTERFACE-level and not type-level — `up` here reaches `down.cddl` and
; `down` reaches back, but no single type is recursive — because that is the case a type-level
; detector would miss.

up = [d: down_leaf]

up_leaf = [n: uint]
